

### CMD: smbclient -L //192.168.10.254 -N
--- rationale: Null-session share enumeration. If anonymous listing works, any LAN host reads share names+comments pre-auth.
session setup failed: NT_STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED
[exit 1]


### CMD: smbclient -L //192.168.10.254 -U guest%
--- rationale: Guest fallback. Windows may refuse null but allow guest; guest+writable share = file drop.

	Sharename       Type      Comment
	---------       ----      -------
	ADMIN$          Disk      Remote Admin
	C$              Disk      Default share
	IPC$            IPC       Remote IPC
	Users           Disk      
SMB1 disabled -- no workgroup available
[exit 0]


### CMD: smbclient -L //192.168.10.254 -U guest% --option=client signing=required
--- rationale: SMB signing posture. Signing NOT required is the precondition for NTLM relay. Pure protocol negotiation - reads no user data.

	Sharename       Type      Comment
	---------       ----      -------
	ADMIN$          Disk      Remote Admin
	C$              Disk      Default share
	IPC$            IPC       Remote IPC
	Users           Disk      
SMB1 disabled -- no workgroup available
[exit 0]


### CMD: smbclient -L //192.168.10.254 -U guest% --option=client max protocol=SMB3
--- rationale: Max dialect negotiation. SMB3 vs SMB1/2 determines relay+downgrade exposure. Protocol handshake only.

	Sharename       Type      Comment
	---------       ----      -------
	ADMIN$          Disk      Remote Admin
	C$              Disk      Default share
	IPC$            IPC       Remote IPC
	Users           Disk      
SMB1 disabled -- no workgroup available
[exit 0]


### CMD: smbclient -L //192.168.10.254 -U guest% --option=client max protocol=NT1
--- rationale: SMB1 explicitly - confirms SMB1 fully disabled (already indicated by 'SMB1 disabled' banner).
lp_load_ex: Max protocol NT1 is less than min protocol SMB2_02.
Protocol negotiation to server 192.168.10.254 (for a protocol between SMB2_02 and NT1) failed: NT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER_MIX
[exit 1]
